<title>USA: Fair skies dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Fair skies dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong ridge of high pressure is expected to dominate Brazil's coffee belt for the next 5-7 days bringing fair and warm weather to the region during the period, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Monday.</p>
<p>Mostly fair skies were observed in main growing areas of the belt over the weekend. Temperatures averaged near normal levels for this time of year with lows ranging from 48-57 F (9-14 C). Some minor growing areas reported lows of 43-49 F (6-9 C).</p>
<p>The outlook calls for mostly fair skies through Friday. Temperatures should remain in the 50's F (10-16 C). Cooler conditions are still expected in higher elevations, although there is no sign of damaging cold, according to WSC. ((Eileen Houlihan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
